\description{
Reproduces \code{sdm.models.KumoTabular(task = "regression")}: each member
predicts 999 quantiles (levels 0.001 to 0.999) of its standardized,
randomly signed target; the sign and the scaling are undone, each
member's grid is sorted, and the members are combined by a trimmed mean
that drops \code{floor(0.2 * n_estimators)} from each tail, level by level.
\code{type = "mean"} is the mean of that grid -- the point estimate NVIDIA's
AutoGluon wrapper reports; \code{"median"} and \code{"quantiles"} interpolate it.
